PLACEHOLDER — this is not a real game executable.

This plain-text file stands in for the real FullFeaturedGame.exe so the
example folder has the layout X-Native's catalog expects: the manifest
(game.json, one folder up) names this file as "game/FullFeaturedGame.exe",
and the catalog only catalogues a manifest game when the named executable
actually exists on disk.

Replace this file with the real FullFeaturedGame.exe to use the example
for real. Until then the catalog still lists the game: a file that is not
a valid PE image is catalogued as a Windows executable with unknown
architecture rather than being dropped.
